       "tabletStyles": {},
       "children": [],
       "innerHTML": "The short version: <strong>the open-notes app has no analytics and no tracking</strong>, and your notes are encrypted on your device before they go anywhere. <strong>This website does use analytics</strong>, as described below. I'm Adam Dawoodjee, and I run both."
      }
     ],
     "blockName": "Intro"
    },
    {
     "attributes": {},
     "baseStyles": {
      "alignItems": "flex-start",
      "boxSizing": "border-box",
      "display": "flex",
      "flexDirection": "column",
      "gap": "16px",
      "maxWidth": "960px",
      "padding": "48px 24px 0",
      "width": "100%"
     },
     "blockId": "a51f815af1",
     "classes": [
      "on-legal"
     ],
     "element": "section",
     "mobileStyles": {
      "padding": "32px 16px 0"
     },
     "tabletStyles": {},
     "children": [
      {
       "attributes": {},
       "baseStyles": {
        "color": "var(--on-text)",
        "fontSize": "28px",
        "fontWeight": "700",
        "letterSpacing": "-0.01em",
        "lineHeight": "1.15",
        "margin": "0"
       },
       "blockId": "6d1adaa21f",
       "classes": [],
       "element": "h2",
       "mobileStyles": {
        "fontSize": "22px"
       },
       "tabletStyles": {
        "fontSize": "24px"
       },
       "children": [],
       "innerHTML": "The app"
      },
      {
       "attributes": {},
       "baseStyles": {
        "color": "var(--on-muted)",
        "fontSize": "19px",
        "lineHeight": "1.6",
        "margin": "0",
        "maxWidth": "680px"
       },
       "blockId": "cccd9d00ed",
       "classes": [],
       "element": "p",
       "mobileStyles": {
        "fontSize": "17px"
       },
       "tabletStyles": {},
       "children": [],
       "innerHTML": "<ul><li><strong>Without an account</strong>, your notes stay on your device. The app sends nothing anywhere.</li><li><strong>With sync on</strong>, you sign in with an email code or with Google. The sync service I run (on Supabase) then holds your email address, your sign-in records, and your notes and folders in encrypted form.</li><li><strong>What the server can and can't see.</strong> Titles, note text and folder names are encrypted on your device with a key only you hold, so neither the server nor I can read them. The server sees what it needs to sync: when notes and folders were created and changed, how folders nest, and flags such as whether a note is in Recently Deleted.</li><li><strong>Signing in with Google</strong> gives the service your email address and the name and picture on your Google account, and Google knows you signed in.</li><li><strong>Deleting your account</strong> in Settings removes it, with your encrypted notes and keys, from the server 30 days later. You can cancel during those 30 days. You can export your notes at any time as a zip of Markdown files.</li><li><strong>If you host your own server</strong>, it's yours, and none of this involves me.</li></ul>"
      }
     ],
     "blockName": "The app"
    },
